index 0000000..e15d36d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/archive/phase_0_1/prompts/REVIEW.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+Act as the independent reviewer for the current milestone. Read PROJECT_BRIEF.md, AGENTS.md, docs/IMPLEMENTATION_CONTRACT.md, docs/HANDOFF.md and the relevant changed files/tests. If you cannot access a file, say so; do not review an imagined implementation.
+
+Do not edit production code. Write a review report or return one for the implementation owner.
+
+Look for material failures in accounting, MTF liabilities/interest/margin, order recovery, data availability timestamps, research leakage, statistical selection, risk constraints, credential boundaries and truthful completion claims. Scale review to the changed scope.
+
+For every finding give:
+- severity and concrete triggering scenario;
+- file/function or design rule involved;
+- expected versus actual behavior;
+- a minimal reproduction or counterexample;
+- the smallest justified correction.
+
+Separate confirmed defects from questions or speculative concerns. Identify tests whose expected values merely repeat the implementation. Do not recommend weakening assertions to make tests pass.
+
+Conclude READY FOR NEXT PHASE, READY WITH NONBLOCKING ITEMS, or NOT READY, with reasons and exact missing evidence. Passing engineering tests does not certify profitability.
